      <abstract>
        <p>This fixture exercises slice 5d: structured bibliography emission as
JATS <monospace>&lt;element-citation&gt;</monospace> (per-field author/title/source/volume/etc.)
plus external-DSL JATS treatment (mermaid/abc as <monospace>&lt;fig&gt;</monospace> with
<monospace>&lt;preformat&gt;</monospace> source preservation).</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>This section cites Smith and Doe <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-Smith2020">Smith2020</xref> and the Jones
field-research textbook <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-Jones2018">Jones2018</xref>. A third citation points
to the diagram-layout paper <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-Brown2021">Brown2021</xref>.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Diagrams</title>
      <p>A Mermaid flowchart with a caption (cross-referenced as <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig:flow">figure 1</xref>):</p>
      <fig id="fig:flow" specific-use="enscribe-dsl-mermaid">
        <label>1</label>
        <caption>
          <p>A simple Mermaid flowchart.</p>
        </caption>
        <alt-text>Mermaid diagram source preserved as preformatted text.</alt-text>
        <preformat preformat-type="mermaid-source">graph TD;
  A[Start] --&gt; B{Decision};
  B --&gt;|yes| C[Do thing];
  B --&gt;|no|  D[Skip];</preformat>
      </fig>
      <p>An ABC music notation snippet with a caption (cross-referenced as
<xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig:tune">figure 2</xref>):</p>
      <fig id="fig:tune" specific-use="enscribe-dsl-abc">
        <label>2</label>
        <caption>
          <p>A short ABC tune.</p>
        </caption>
        <alt-text>Abc diagram source preserved as preformatted text.</alt-text>
        <preformat preformat-type="abc-source">X:1
T:Twinkle Twinkle
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
C C G G | A A G2 | F F E E | D D C2 |</preformat>
      </fig>
    </sec>
  </body>
